What is Green Semiconductor Energy and Natural Resources Technology?
The market encompasses advanced semiconductor devices designed for low‑power renewable energy conversion, waste‑heat harvesting, and sustainable resource‑extraction technologies. Core products include wide‑bandgap power chips (such as silicon‑carbide (SiC) and gallium‑nitride (GaN)), photovoltaic‑integrated circuits, smart‑grid micro‑controllers, and sensor platforms that enable efficient monitoring of water, minerals, and carbon cycles.
